# 057 — Viewer `view` — done

**Type:** feature · **Priority:** P0 · **Status:** done (2026-10-04) · **Blocked by:** 054 · **Roadmap:** track G, tools plan §4.3

Formerly tools-branch 037.

## Problem

There is no way to read a text file on the disk; the first text tool should work on today's read-only VFS.

## Plan

- `view <path>`: text mode (UTF-8, wrap on/off, ↑/↓/PgUp/PgDn/Home/End, search F7 / Shift+F7 next, go to line) and hex mode (F4: offset, 16 bytes, character column). Reads on demand by offset, never loads the whole file; a line index is built incrementally.
- Status line: name, size, position, mode; F-key bar; Esc or F10 exits.
- The core (line index, search, hex formatting) is shared with `fm` and `edit`.

## Acceptance criteria

- QEMU suite `tools`: `view` opens a text with Cyrillic and a binary; screendump checks; search finds a word on a later page.

## Related

[docs/tools](../docs/tools/README.md) §4.3.

## Resolution

`libmind/src/tui/viewer.rs`: a `Source` trait (size, read at offset) and a `Cache` that keeps a window of the file in a caller's buffer and decodes UTF-8 characters at any offset (invalid bytes become U+FFFD). `Viewer` lays out text by visual rows (wrapping at the screen width, tabs to 8, or unwrapped with ←/→ horizontal shift and a `»` mark), scrolls up and down by rows and pages, finds the last page, counts line numbers incrementally from the nearest known point, shows a hex dump (offset, 16 bytes, characters), searches ignoring case for any letters (Latin, Cyrillic) across window boundaries and wraps to the start, highlights the match, goes to a line, a hex offset or a percentage, and draws a status line (name, line, offset, percentage, size, mode), the F-key bar, a help box and input dialogs. The `view` program opens a file through VFS with a 64 KiB window and logs its position. Tests: `tests/viewer_host.rs` (5 tests: paging, end, line numbers both ways, wrapping, horizontal shift, hex, go to, search including Cyrillic case and wrap, not found, invalid UTF-8 and tabs) and the QEMU suite `tools` (a 300-line Russian text: first page, status, page down, F7 search in upper case, End, Esc; hex mode on `kernel.elf`; a missing file; no leaked memory).
